1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,367
<i> We already know everything.</i>

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,033
<i> How could you do this to us?</i>

3
00:00:03,167 --> 00:00:04,733
<i> You really need to leave now.</i>

4
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:05,700
<i> They're here.</i>

5
00:00:05,833 --> 00:00:07,467
<i>We can't just keep
hiding from them.</i>

6
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,367
<i> Parak, come out of there!</i>

7
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,500
<i> No matter what happens,</i>

8
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:12,700
<i> don't dare make a sound, okay?</i>

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,167
<i>You really didn't tell
Ma'am Clarissa about it</i>

10
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,467
<i>during your arraignment, Major?</i>

11
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,933
<i>Attorney said I'll be able
to post bail.</i>

12
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:25,167
<i>You don't have any
identification on him, Major?</i>

13
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,067
<i> None, but I'm sure...</i>

14
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,667
<i>the syndicates sent him
to silence me.</i>

15
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:30,767
<i> Major!</i>

16
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,567
<i>Make sure no one recognizes you.</i>

17
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,967
<i>If they do, I'll personally
finish you off!</i>

18
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:36,300
<i> Are you done with Parak?</i>

19
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:38,333
<i>- He's slippery, Boss.
- He's all alone!</i>

20
00:00:38,467 --> 00:00:39,433
<i>Looks like he has someone
with him, Boss.</i>

21
00:00:39,567 --> 00:00:40,400
<i> Someone's helping him.</i>

22
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:41,500
<i> I'll handle it!</i>

23
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:42,900
<i> Godfather!</i>

24
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:44,367
<i> No matter what happens,</i>

25
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,500
<i>don't come out,
and don't scream.</i>

26
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,433
<i> Your companion's good.</i>

27
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:53,600
<i> Slippery!</i>

28
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:54,800
<i> Where's Diego?</i>

29
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:56,633
<i> The syndicate got him!</i>

30
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:57,967
<i> Come on, let's go.</i>

31
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:21,133
Be careful.

32
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:25,733
Where's Godfather?

33
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:30,433
He was just there!

34
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:32,367
Andrew, he couldn't have
gone far.

35
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,467
He wouldn't be able to.

36
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,000
He was barely conscious earlier.

37
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,033
Joey, if he didn't escape,

38
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:51,233
that means the syndicate
took him.

39
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,767
Andrew, we need to call
the police.

40
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:00,367
Maybe we can still
catch up to Godfather.

41
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,467
Joey, Joey, relax.
Okay?

42
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,967
You won't be able to think
clearly if you're like this.

43
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:06,900
I'll handle this.

44
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:09,933
Mr. Miguel Delgado,
how do you plead?

45
00:02:10,067 --> 00:02:11,833
Not guilty, Your Honor.

46
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:14,167
We move for the grant of bail.

47
00:02:15,067 --> 00:02:17,167
My client is
a former police officer

48
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:19,733
with a very clean record.

49
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:21,800
He is not a flight risk.

50
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:24,667
Just earlier, there was an
attempt on his life

51
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:28,167
inside this very courthouse.

52
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,267
This shows the level of danger

53
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,300
he is facing while in custody.

54
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:37,467
Your Honor, the evidence
of guilt is strong.

55
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,967
The gun recovered
from the accused

56
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:41,267
matched the ballistics

57
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,467
of the bullet
that killed Ramon Orbos.

58
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,400
Wait.

59
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:45,667
I didn't kill Ramon!

60
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,233
Order in court.

61
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,867
And also, Your Honor,

62
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,233
the alleged attempt on the life
of the accused,

63
00:02:51,367 --> 00:02:52,833
while unfortunate,

64
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:55,933
is not legal grounds for bail.

65
00:02:58,567 --> 00:03:01,267
Bail is a matter of right

66
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:05,567
only in cases not punishable
by reclusion perpetua.

67
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:08,833
The accused is charged
with murder.

68
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:10,700
Counsel, you know murder

69
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:13,333
is punishable by reclusion
perpetua.

70
00:03:13,467 --> 00:03:14,933
The law is clear.

71
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:17,800
Bail is determined by the weight
of the evidence

72
00:03:17,933 --> 00:03:19,233
and the nature of the offense,

73
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:21,200
not external threats.

74
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:24,067
If the accused fears
for his life,

75
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:27,633
perhaps he may request
a protection order instead.

76
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:31,267
But granting the bail...

77
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:34,000
is discretionary upon the Court,

78
00:03:34,133 --> 00:03:35,933
considering the charge

79
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:40,367
is punishable
by reclusion perpetua.

80
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,233
Therefore...

81
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:46,633
the motion for bail is denied.

82
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:50,433
The accused shall be committed
to the provincial jail...

83
00:03:50,567 --> 00:03:52,933
effective immediately,
pending trial.

84
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,133
So ordered.

85
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,400
Judge, I'm innocent!

86
00:03:58,533 --> 00:04:00,200
- Sheriff.
- Ah, Attorney!

87
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:02,267
Serve the commitment order.

88
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:13,667
Cruz, take care of my family.

89
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,533
You inform them.

90
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:18,167
But don't tell them
what happened to me earlier.

91
00:04:44,167 --> 00:04:45,267
Joey!

92
00:04:46,833 --> 00:04:48,100
Joey!

93
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:50,900
I've been calling you.
You keep canceling my calls!

94
00:04:51,033 --> 00:04:52,533
Hey, what happened?

95
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:55,233
Are you okay?

96
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:58,333
We went...

97
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:00,733
to Joey's godfather.

98
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:01,900
There was a shootout.

99
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:03,767
We got trapped.

100
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:07,233
So after you left,
you ran into trouble?

101
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:20,967
Trouble?

102
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,367
Where is Major Aglipay?

103
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,967
He's missing.

104
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,667
You wouldn't have been in danger

105
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,700
if you hadn't snuck out.

106
00:05:30,833 --> 00:05:32,633
Hey, can you please stop?

107
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,300
That's enough.

108
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:38,033
Look at Joey.

109
00:05:38,167 --> 00:05:40,267
She's been through enough
already.

110
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,200
Don't add to it.

111
00:05:50,967 --> 00:05:52,633
Clarissa...

112
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:55,567
I'm assigning you
to Barangay Luna

113
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:59,400
for our next Care on Wheels
mission, okay?

114
00:05:59,533 --> 00:06:00,800
Me personally?

115
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:02,233
Of course.

116
00:06:02,367 --> 00:06:03,600
But don't worry, okay?

117
00:06:03,733 --> 00:06:04,533
Lorna will help you

118
00:06:04,667 --> 00:06:06,833
with the clearances and permits.

119
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,300
Thank you, Ma'am.

120
00:06:09,433 --> 00:06:10,367
- Don't mention it.
- Three people were killed

121
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,600
<i>in a break-in and shooting
incident</i>

122
00:06:12,733 --> 00:06:14,433
<i> at a residential establishment</i>

123
00:06:14,567 --> 00:06:17,167
<i> in Barangay 198 in Manila.</i>

124
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,467
<i> The homeowner was identified</i>

125
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,900
<i> as Police Major Diego Aglipay</i>

126
00:06:21,033 --> 00:06:23,367
<i>of the Metro Norte
Police Command.</i>

127
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:26,300
<i>Authorities are still
investigating</i>

128
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:28,333
<i>the full details
of the incident.</i>

129
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:29,600
<i> There is still no confirmation</i>

130
00:06:29,733 --> 00:06:32,733
<i>on Major Aglipay's whereabouts
following the incident.</i>

131
00:06:32,867 --> 00:06:35,167
Sir, can you call my child?

132
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,800
I know they are going to meet.

133
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:39,000
He's her godfather!

134
00:06:39,133 --> 00:06:40,533
Come on, take him already!
Put him inside!

135
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,200
Sir! Sir...

136
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:45,000
Take him in.
You talk too much.

137
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:46,267
Sir...

138
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,700
Ma'am...
Ma'am...

139
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:55,967
I'll just get my uniform first.

140
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,633
- Okay.
- Go on.

141
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,133
Lorna.

142
00:07:02,267 --> 00:07:03,367
Come here.

143
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,900
We need to sort out
these files I found.

144
00:07:09,667 --> 00:07:10,700
Cruz?

145
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,067
<i> Ma'am Clarissa...</i>

146
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,800
I'm sorry for calling.

147
00:07:14,967 --> 00:07:16,367
Is this about Diego?

148
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,567
What happened?

149
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,833
I don't know.

150
00:07:18,967 --> 00:07:21,300
I haven't heard anything yet,
Ma'am.

151
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:22,500
I saw it on TV.

152
00:07:22,633 --> 00:07:23,900
They said his house
was broken into.

153
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:25,200
Now he's missing.

154
00:07:25,333 --> 00:07:27,500
Miguel needs to know this, Cruz.

155
00:07:27,633 --> 00:07:30,267
That's actually why I'm calling,
Ma'am.

156
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:33,000
The arraignment hearing for
Major just finished.

157
00:07:33,133 --> 00:07:35,400
He wasn't granted bail.

158
00:07:35,533 --> 00:07:38,033
He's being transferred
to the provincial jail now.

159
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,500
What?

160
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,033
Sir...

161
00:07:43,167 --> 00:07:44,700
I need to talk to my family.

162
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:47,000
They don't know I'm here.

163
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,867
Sir...

164
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,800
I beg you.

165
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:57,233
Sir!

166
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,667
Sir, I need to talk
to my family!

167
00:08:01,633 --> 00:08:03,267
Sir!

168
00:08:44,067 --> 00:08:46,967
Joey, that's enough.

169
00:08:48,267 --> 00:08:50,600
I'll monitor everything.

170
00:08:51,933 --> 00:08:54,733
If there's any development,

171
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:57,200
I'll let you know, okay?

172
00:08:58,267 --> 00:09:00,500
But for now, please...

173
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:03,700
Get some rest.

174
00:09:05,433 --> 00:09:07,600
I can't rest anyway.

175
00:09:38,367 --> 00:09:40,067
Hello, Mom?

176
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:42,367
Have you heard
what happened to Godfather?

177
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:44,933
<i> Yes, my child, I saw it.</i>

178
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:46,733
Wherever your godfather
is right now,

179
00:09:46,867 --> 00:09:48,667
I just hope he's safe.

180
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:52,467
<i> Joey, I don't understand...</i>

181
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:55,600
<i>why the bad news keeps coming
one after another.</i>

182
00:09:55,733 --> 00:09:57,567
What do you mean?

183
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:01,333
Your father wasn't granted bail.

184
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,533
<i> As usual, no one told us.</i>

185
00:10:03,667 --> 00:10:05,033
His arraignment hearing
was earlier.

186
00:10:05,167 --> 00:10:06,933
Cruz just called me.

187
00:10:07,067 --> 00:10:09,433
<i>He's being transferred
to the provincial jail.</i>

188
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:12,367
My child...

189
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:14,633
<i> What is happening to us?</i>

190
00:10:27,933 --> 00:10:29,300
Mom, please don't overthink,
okay?

191
00:10:29,433 --> 00:10:30,700
I'll just head over there.

192
00:10:30,833 --> 00:10:32,133
We'll go see Dad.

193
00:10:32,267 --> 00:10:33,933
Please don't overthink.

194
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,567
Okay, my child.

195
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,367
I love you, Mom.

196
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,033
Okay.

197
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,600
Dad...

198
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,867
Dad...

199
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,533
Cellmate...

200
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,700
Is there somewhere
I can make a call here?

201
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,300
Why are you asking me?

202
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:43,167
What do you think I am?
A smuggler?

203
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,800
I know you can do it.

204
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,467
I'll double the payment.

205
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,667
What if that's a setup...

206
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,833
and you're just going to
rat us out?

207
00:11:54,967 --> 00:11:56,667
Wait, I'm not an informant.

208
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,433
My papers are clean, even if you
have me picked up and checked.

209
00:11:59,567 --> 00:12:01,200
If I find out
you're screwing me over,

210
00:12:01,333 --> 00:12:02,600
I'll crush you.

211
00:12:02,733 --> 00:12:04,333
Buddy, I'm not with
any syndicate.

212
00:12:04,467 --> 00:12:06,567
I just need to talk
to my daughter.

213
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:19,833
What?

214
00:12:19,967 --> 00:12:21,800
You really don't recognize me?

215
00:12:21,933 --> 00:12:24,400
Because I remember that face of
yours very clearly.

216
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:25,967
I know you're a cop.

217
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,233
I'm the robber you chased down

218
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:29,933
until I ended up in prison.

219
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:33,567
Now I finally get to have
my revenge on you.

220
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:38,933
It's dangerous
in the provincial jail.

221
00:12:39,067 --> 00:12:40,000
Oppa, do you understand?

222
00:12:40,133 --> 00:12:41,767
There are killers there.

223
00:12:43,633 --> 00:12:44,833
What do you want to do?

224
00:12:44,967 --> 00:12:47,933
Find the video
and Joey's godfather?

225
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,500
But both are gone.

226
00:12:50,733 --> 00:12:53,000
We don't even know
where Major Aglipay is.

227
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,867
Andrew...

228
00:12:58,467 --> 00:13:02,233
Maybe you can expose
what really happened...

229
00:13:02,367 --> 00:13:04,800
how Godfather helped
the syndicate.

230
00:13:04,933 --> 00:13:05,767
Maybe that's the only thing

231
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,867
that can really help Dad.

232
00:13:10,267 --> 00:13:12,500
Joey, we don't have
a solid evidence.

233
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:15,833
I didn't get any direct
admission

234
00:13:15,967 --> 00:13:18,033
from Major Aglipay on record.

235
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:20,467
I can't release an exposé
without that.

236
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,567
Then maybe you can at least
give people an idea?

237
00:13:22,733 --> 00:13:24,233
Isn't that what you do?

238
00:13:24,367 --> 00:13:27,300
You give ideas
to your subscribers.

239
00:13:27,433 --> 00:13:28,433
Don't you always update them

240
00:13:28,567 --> 00:13:30,600
about the cases
you're following?

241
00:13:31,567 --> 00:13:35,433
Joey, now is not the time, okay?

242
00:13:37,267 --> 00:13:39,600
Especially after
what just happened.

243
00:13:39,733 --> 00:13:44,567
Joey, we need solid evidence
against the syndicates.

244
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:45,500
Otherwise, everything
we're doing...

245
00:13:45,633 --> 00:13:47,567
will just go to waste.

246
00:13:48,633 --> 00:13:50,333
Is that really it, Andrew?

247
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:54,167
Or you just don't want to do it
because you're a coward?

248
00:13:55,667 --> 00:13:58,200
Looks like luck is on my side.

249
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:00,433
Who would've thought we'd all
end up together here?

250
00:14:00,567 --> 00:14:02,600
The world really does
come full circle.

251
00:14:12,167 --> 00:14:14,033
Hey! What's going on there?

252
00:14:14,167 --> 00:14:16,033
Sir, we're just having some fun.

253
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:18,433
Just welcoming our new cellmate!

254
00:14:18,567 --> 00:14:19,933
He's new!

255
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,267
Cut it out!

256
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,500
Break it up!

257
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:23,767
Yes, Sir.

258
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,333
That's enough!

259
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,367
Be careful, Joey.

260
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:39,267
- I'm not a coward.
- You are a coward.

261
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:42,667
Just admit it, you don't really
care about my father!

262
00:14:44,333 --> 00:14:45,300
All you care about,

263
00:14:45,433 --> 00:14:48,367
are your subscribers
and your show!

264
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,467
That's what this is really
about, isn't it?

265
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,833
Can you...

266
00:14:52,633 --> 00:14:55,133
Can you stop being irrational?

267
00:14:56,967 --> 00:15:00,233
This is bigger than your pain.

268
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:04,267
I know you're upset.

269
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,900
That's why you're emotional.

270
00:15:06,033 --> 00:15:07,567
Now, just take a step back.

271
00:15:08,567 --> 00:15:10,300
Joey, just...

272
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:12,733
talk to me when...

273
00:15:12,867 --> 00:15:14,167
when you're okay.

274
00:15:16,533 --> 00:15:18,233
Just get some rest.

275
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:59,167
He's about to die.

276
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:00,567
Why did you even bring him here?

277
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,800
I'm not done with him yet.

278
00:16:07,567 --> 00:16:09,433
No wonder from the very
beginning,

279
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,700
I already had
a bad feeling about you...

280
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:14,400
because there's something
twisted deep inside you!

281
00:16:19,033 --> 00:16:21,400
Who was with you earlier
at your house?

282
00:16:21,533 --> 00:16:23,967
I know someone's helping you!

283
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,667
Who are they?

284
00:16:37,067 --> 00:16:39,267
Just a tip, Parak.

285
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:42,367
Make it easy for yourself.

286
00:16:42,533 --> 00:16:44,967
If you're hiding something,
tell us now.

287
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:47,933
It's the right time to confess,

288
00:16:48,067 --> 00:16:52,033
and maybe we'll spare you.

289
00:16:57,133 --> 00:16:59,067
<i> I trusted you, Godfather!</i>

290
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,433
<i>Because I thought you were
a good man!</i>

291
00:17:00,567 --> 00:17:02,200
<i>I thought you were going
to help my father!</i>

292
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:03,267
<i> But you're actually the reason</i>

293
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,100
<i> he ended up in prison?</i>

294
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:07,167
<i> How could you do this to us?</i>

295
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,767
<i> We already know everything.</i>

296
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:11,233
<i> So if I were you,</i>

297
00:17:11,367 --> 00:17:13,167
<i> I'd confess.</i>

298
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,000
Come in.

299
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:33,067
Jin Ho.

300
00:17:38,067 --> 00:17:39,400
Joey...

301
00:17:44,633 --> 00:17:46,400
About earlier...

302
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,967
I'm sorry.

303
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:55,467
I was, you know, frustrated.

304
00:17:56,767 --> 00:17:58,133
I'm just...

305
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:01,300
Scared for you.

306
00:18:01,433 --> 00:18:02,733
It's okay.

307
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:05,367
I understand
where you're coming from.

308
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:08,767
Let me know when you're leaving.

309
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,033
I'll drive you.

310
00:18:10,167 --> 00:18:12,500
Actually, I don't feel
like going anymore.

311
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:16,700
What happened?

312
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:18,233
Nothing.

313
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:22,400
I've got no good news anyway.

314
00:18:23,567 --> 00:18:25,500
I failed my father.

315
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,600
You know what?

316
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,767
I think I'd rather look for
Godfather Diego.

317
00:18:41,967 --> 00:18:43,500
Because I keep thinking...

318
00:18:44,467 --> 00:18:45,767
What if he got away?

319
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:46,867
What if he's just hiding?

320
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,367
What if he's just protecting me
in his own way?

321
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:52,300
I'll ask you again.

322
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:55,067
Who was with you earlier?

323
00:18:55,233 --> 00:18:56,667
Answer me!

324
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:58,433
You're still being stubborn?

325
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,333
You know, if you could see

326
00:19:21,467 --> 00:19:24,700
your faces in the mirror,

327
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:27,300
you'd realize
how stupid you look.

328
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:29,600
You're all on edge, aren't you?

329
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,367
Waiting for me to talk...

330
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,500
waiting for
what I'm going to say.

331
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,033
What do you think, huh?

332
00:19:38,167 --> 00:19:40,433
That you're lucky?

333
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:43,333
What? You can't fool me!

334
00:19:45,967 --> 00:19:48,367
Let me make this clear to you.

335
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,700
I regret...

336
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:55,567
ever getting involved
with your syndicate!

337
00:19:57,633 --> 00:19:59,133
I even betrayed...

338
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:01,200
my own friend for you?

339
00:20:01,333 --> 00:20:04,500
You're worthless!
You're demons!

340
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:08,267
And you, what are you saying?

341
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:10,333
You'll forgive me?

342
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,667
Then keep your forgiveness.

343
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,133
I don't need it.

344
00:20:15,267 --> 00:20:17,867
I'd rather die!

345
00:20:23,733 --> 00:20:25,567
I've seen groups like the one

346
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:27,733
Diego got involved with.

347
00:20:31,767 --> 00:20:34,700
They don't let betrayers slide.

348
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,900
They have their ways.

349
00:20:43,767 --> 00:20:45,300
Torture.

350
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:48,267
Silence.

351
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:51,567
They make people disappear.

352
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:54,833
No one ever finds them.

353
00:20:57,733 --> 00:20:59,467
So you're saying...

354
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:02,433
He's really gone?

355
00:21:41,267 --> 00:21:43,567
But we can't just focus on
damage control.

356
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:44,567
What do you mean?

357
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:45,667
We have to control
the narrative.

358
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,800
I know everything now.

359
00:21:46,933 --> 00:21:48,400
Miguel, there's something
you need to know.

360
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:50,467
Where is Major Aglipay?

361
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:55,000
The corruption of these
syndicates is this blatant.

362
00:21:55,133 --> 00:21:56,467
Once everything is exposed,

363
00:21:56,600 --> 00:22:00,233
I promise you,
heads will roll.

364
00:22:00,367 --> 00:22:02,600
Amazing!

365
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:03,933
She was an informant?

366
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:04,833
Yes.

367
00:22:04,967 --> 00:22:06,033
That's why they used her
against him.

368
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:07,200
You again?

369
00:22:07,333 --> 00:22:08,367
We won't get anything
staying inside.

370
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:09,633
I spoke to a woman.

371
00:22:09,767 --> 00:22:12,233
She clearly knows something,
but her lips are sealed.

372
00:22:12,367 --> 00:22:14,033
You just don't have the finesse,
do you?

373
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:15,000
I'll handle it.

374
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,700
Let me talk.

375
00:22:16,833 --> 00:22:19,300
Oh, he's already inside.
